   378	/**
   379	 * M11-2 P3.3 — the memory twin of the claim, lease-renewal, completion and housekeeping writers in
   380	 * `db.ts`. Same semantics throughout: claim order (earliest due, loop-enabled, not already in
   381	 * flight), budget-then-claim sequencing (a refused claim spends nothing), and the same token-fenced
   382	 * lease/completion writes.
   383	 *
   384	 * **No true parallelism stands in for `FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED` here, and that IS the whole
   385	 * guarantee.** `claimNextWakeup` below has no `await` between its scan and its write — this file's
   386	 * house style, stated at the top ("one synchronous section, no `await` between the check and the
   387	 * write") — so two "concurrent" calls in a test (e.g. `Promise.all([claimNextWakeup(...),
   388	 * claimNextWakeup(...)])`) still run their synchronous bodies to completion one at a time: JS has one
